        "id": 1002609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-05T20:08:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is an asynchronous call anyway.  Why do we need this extra step.\n\nCan\u0027t we just block and return the contents after the init is done?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 499,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 499,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6eb1e0c4_a29b15af",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/IRadio.hal",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 499,
      "author": {
        "id": 1156349
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-09T10:22:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently, telephony doesn’t get SIM phonebook at boot up, then the “initdone” isn\u0027t necessary during the whole process. But once a new requirement to query the record immediately after SIM ready, then it rather need this indication to ensure modem side is ready. Otherwise if modem is not ready, it will get failure immediately, or if blocking till ready, the wakelock from RILJ might time out.\n\nFurthermore, how about renaming the ”phonebookInitDone” to “SimPhoneBookReady” to exactly express this indication, just like existing SIM ready indication? Only after this explicit indication, the client could load SIM phonebook gracefully.",
      "parentUuid": "28a696a3_7f210000",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 499,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 499,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f59acec_f62ce419",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/IRadio.hal",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 499,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-10T02:43:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Fei.  Discussed this with Ajay earlier today and I think we have a better compromise:\n\nTurn this into the real get + changed-notification model.\n\nRemove the language that it \"can only be used after receiving..\".  Before the phonebook is read this would just return an empty set.  When it\u0027s ready we\u0027ll get a unsol notification that the phonebook has changed (and if the phonebook does change for some reason, you can send that again to trigger a re-fetch from the AP).\n\nThis has the same semantics from your side but adds value in the unsol indication from our POV and fits the existing models better.\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "6eb1e0c4_a29b15af",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 499,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 499,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e422df39_7376c964",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/IRadio.hal",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 499,
      "author": {
        "id": 1156349
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-15T07:29:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, this is good, RIL could return empty if SIM phonebook module is not ready. And once ready, we will send one notification to telephony.\n\nOne concern is that, if telephony/UI update one PBM record, then modem will send one indication after update, how will AP handle it since AP already has the valid cache?",
      "parentUuid": "1f59acec_f62ce419",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 499,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 499,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "135bd193_a80c7059",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/IRadio.hal",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 499,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-16T22:41:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The AP should refill their cache.  This can be done on a side thread so it doesn\u0027t interrupt callers and then swapped in when ready.  We may need API to let apps know things have changed.",
      "parentUuid": "e422df39_7376c964",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 499,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 499,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
