      },
      "lineNbr": 507,
      "author": {
        "id": 1156349
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-09T10:22:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently other async APIs like startNetworkScan don’t have the token, so we follow the same. And in qcril/QMI, no token are used either. \n\nIn case of multiple or duplicated requests on one sub, they will be queued and returned only once after completion, see mAdnLoadingWaiters in https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/opt/telephony/+/1440475/18/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/uicc/SimPhoneBookRecordCache.java#144.\n\nBesides, if adding the token, RIL could just store the token but almost does nothing. So can we keep the current design?",
      "parentUuid": "5b85860e_aa52c84f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 507,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 507,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
